## Context

[Review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-split) found distinct parser and booking-form hint failures merged together.
The old [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) remains an immutable historical record.
This proposal would supersede it after the support desk approves it.

## Proposed decision

Read the report, resolve the tenant's locale and form version, and identify the failure path using channel and reproducible evidence.
Merge only when the reports share a verified cause; differing subjects may still describe the same cause.
A matching subject alone is insufficient. Intake tags and browser locale are clues, not the cause classifier.
Unknown tenants and uncertain failures remain separate for investigation rather than being merged by default.

## Consequences

Triage takes more reading but preserves separate engineering work and accurate per-cause impact.
Keep received and merged timestamps separate, count report IDs once across overlapping exports, and preserve evidence and uncertainty.
Review the decision against future rendered tables and reproduction results, rather than allowing accepted prose to overrule current evidence.

